Aerie-Purpose: Show the page in the rounded Aerie card: force the rounded frame, take the card radius from radius-xl and hide the card's outline when the theme asks for no border.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (multi_contents_view.cc, contents_container_view.cc, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/views/side_panel (side_panel.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #178. Every decision is one call into the overlay, chrome/browser/ui/views/aerie_frame
(frame_tint_enabled.h), which is false for any window that is not a normal window with the sidebar
layout, so Helium's own radius, pref and outline are untouched everywhere else.

- multi_contents_view.cc: the rounded frame is on whatever kHeliumRoundedFrame says while the tint
  is on. This is the only reader of that pref; every other site (the layouts, the infobar, the drop
  target, ContentsContainerView::should_round_contents_) asks MultiContentsView::ShouldUseRoundedFrame().
- contents_container_view.cc: the card's corner radii are radius-xl (14) while the tint is on, and
  its outline is hidden when the theme's card-border token is 0 px (Vivid). A theme that asks for a
  border keeps Helium's one-pixel stroke until slice I (themes) gives it the token colour and width.
- side_panel.cc: the side panel next to the card takes the same radius.


